{"reference":"Isaiah 17","book":"Isaiah","chapter":17,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Within Isaiah’s Oracles","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Isaiah 17 belongs within a wider sequence in which the book speaks judgment not only against Judah and Israel but also against foreign nations. Across that wider setting, powerful peoples are not treated as beyond accountability; the book also looks ahead to nations learning, worshiping, and sharing in restoration. This broader pattern helps place the chapter’s warnings about Damascus, Ephraim, and threatening nations within a book that addresses both Israel and the nations.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_017_85f9ee38139a77b222c96a99"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}